Subject: avcodec/me_cmp: Avoid GCC 14 loop vectorization ICE.

The pinned Steam Runtime SDK's GCC 14.2 crashes in prepare_cmp_insn
when compiling nsse16_c and vsad8_c for the x86-64 baseline with loop
vectorization.
FFmpeg now enables this optimization, exposing GCC PR124555.

Disable only loop vectorization in this file on GCC 14/x86-64.
Keep other files, assembly implementations and compilers unchanged.

https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=124555

diff --git a/libavcodec/me_cmp.c b/libavcodec/me_cmp.c
--- a/libavcodec/me_cmp.c
+++ b/libavcodec/me_cmp.c
@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "config_components.h"

+#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__) && __GNUC__ == 14 && ARCH_X86_64
+/* GCC PR124555: vector abs expansion can ICE without SSE4 support. */
+#pragma GCC optimize("no-tree-loop-vectorize")
+#endif
+
 static int sse4_c(MPVEncContext *unused, const uint8_t *pix1, const uint8_t *pix2,
                   ptrdiff_t stride, int h)
 {
